WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.868
-Welcome back. I'm here
with our pal Dolly Parton.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:06.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:10.567
-Dolly, you're one of the most
adored people on the planet.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:13.100
And there's so many stories
about you, about your career

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.267
on the Internet,
and I thought maybe tonight

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:17.200
we can clear up
a few rumors or truths

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.234
and just see
what's real and what's not.

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:22.067
-Okay.
-Alright, good.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.667
Okay.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.501
In honor of our song
and your special,

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.200
let's start with
a Christmas one.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.434
During the holidays,
you have a Christmas tree

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:31.968
in every room of your house
and you dress up as Santa

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:33.501
to give out gifts
to your family.

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:35.667
-I do. That's true.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:36.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.601
Well, see I-I'm very big
in my family,

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:40.100
all my little nieces and nephews

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.100
and now my little
grand-nieces and nephews.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.601
And so I go pick them up,
after I got the money to do it,

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:49.367
in a limousine,
but it's like our sleigh.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.000
So I go get them
in my Santa suit,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000
pick them up, they come to my
house for a day and a night.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.234
And then I have an elevator
in my house

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:59.534
that I've had painted
like a chimney down under.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:03.300
And so I come down the elevator
in my Santa suit with my bag

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.234
and they're all down
in the basement.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:06.534
-Is that right?
You brought us a photo.

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:08.300
You brought a photo.
-Oh, yeah. Oh, you have that?

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.901
Yeah.
They had asked me about it.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.400
But this is like --
Over here --

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.534
-[ Audience awws ]
-Oh my gosh.

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:14.000
-There's fire there.
-How cool is this?

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.133
-That's tons of them. That's
just one of the little pictures.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.534
Hey, and this little fella
plays the elf

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:20.267
in our "Magic Mountain
Christmas."

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.567
-Does he really?
-Yeah.

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:22.901
-Look out for the elf, okay?

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:24.667
-But anyway -- So I dress up
and take them around.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:25.834
They spend the night with me.

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:27.234
We do cookies
and that fun stuff.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:28.868
-Of course you do that.
Do you think

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.400
of all the ideas
for Dollywood, by the way?

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.400
Because every second
is thought of.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.334
Every corner is thought of.
I loved it so much.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.801
You were probably like, "Jimmy,
stop talking about Dollywood."

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.367
-Well, you can.
I'm very proud of it.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:42.167
But, no, I have so many
wonderful creative people.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:45.467
But, yeah, I'm very involved
in what goes on at Dollywood.

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.067
-I loved it. I loved
every second of that place.

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:49.400
Go to Dollywood.
By the way, that roller coaster.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.701
I didn't get a chance to tell
you. It scared me so much.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:54.234
I almost died on the roller
coaster, from scared.

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:55.767
I got on this roller coaster.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:58.000
Normally it goes like --
[ Ticking ]

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.133
And you get scared. You're like,
"Oh, it's gonna be good."

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.367
Now, this thing -- I think
it's called the Lightning Rod.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.000
It goes -- Zzhhooo!

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.501
And I thought it was broken.
I thought it was broken.

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:08.734
I'm like -- [ Screams ]

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.534
I scream louder than anyone.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:12.300
This kid's telling me
to calm down behind me

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.167
like, "Calm down, buddy."
I went, "Ohh."

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.634
Anyway, it was --

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.100
-Molly loves
the roller coasters, too.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.267
She was late for the show

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.367
'cause she wants
to ride them all.

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:20.567
-It's the greatest thing.

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:22.067
-We talk about that
in the show with her.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.467
-Okay. How about this?
You once entered

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:27.901
a Dolly Parton
look-alike contest and lost.

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:30.334
-Yeah. I thought it'd be fun.

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:32.834
They give you free drinks.
You don't really win anything.

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:35.000
So, some friends of ours,
we thought it'd be funny,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.567
so I just overexaggerated,

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.534
put a bigger beauty mark,
bigger hair,

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:39.868
bigger, you know, everything.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.400
And I walked across the stage,

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.067
and I got a little
trickle of applause.

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:44.834
So I lost the contest,

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.968
but we had a big time
because of it.

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:48.267
They didn't even consider me.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.767
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:52.567
-Weren't even on the list.
-It was Halloween. You know?

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:55.667
Everybody was out.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.534
-You sleep in your makeup
in case

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.467
you ever need
to evacuate the house

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.367
in the middle of the night.
That's not true.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.634
-That is true.

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:06.133
It's true when I'm in L.A.,

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:07.834
because they have
so many earthquakes

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:09.501
and I'm always scared to death,
you know,

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.968
that there's gonna be one
in the middle of the night.

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:14.501
And I don't want to be out
in the street, you know,

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:17.200
with stuff coming around
and the TV cameras out there.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.634
So I leave my makeup on
out there

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:23.734
and I leave my wig on
a nightstand or, you know --

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:25.534
Or either I fix my hair
a little bit

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:27.334
to make sure
I'm not gonna look too bad.

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:29.534
So that's true.
-So you always look like

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:32.567
a million bucks. Wow.
-I don't know that.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:35.167
That's how much it's cost me
to look like this.

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:38.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.767
-This one seems interesting
to me.

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:42.400
You bought your family's
first TV

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.234
after winning
a greasy-pole climbing contest.

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:48.434
-Well, I was 10 years old,
and I started --

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:49.868
When I was singing.
-Wow.

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:51.834
-On a local
radio and television show.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:53.200
And I was a little ol' tomboy

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.601
because I grew up
with all them brothers.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.100
You know, there's 12 of us kids,

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.167
and we were all just
wild little mountain kids.

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.334
So, anyway,
I knew how to climb a tree,

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:02.033
and this show that I was on,

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:06.234
they had a show that I was
singing on down in Sevierville.

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.067
and they had a greasy pole

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:09.868
at this theater
where we were singing,

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:12.767
and at the top of the pole --
They had it stripped down.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:15.200
And if you climbed it --
And there's $100

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.133
or a few hundred dollars,
whatever it was --

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:20.200
I don't remember now --
at the top of the pole,

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.567
and nobody could climb it.

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:25.734
So I was on a little break
and I kind of rolled around

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.200
in the dirt, a little gravel,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.667
and got a little bit of dirt
on me,

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:31.634
and I climbed up that pole
and I got that money.

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:34.467
And they were mad --
because I was an entertainer --

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.033
that it was rigged somehow.

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:37.501
And the guy
that ran the show said,

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:40.234
"How in the hell
can you rig a greasy pole?"

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:42.234
And so he says,
"She's getting the money."

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:46.100
So, I was singing already on TV,
and we didn't even have a TV.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.467
So I paid down on the TV.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:52.033
We got a TV in our house.
And nobody in our area had a TV.

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:53.701
And my daddy worked hard.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.701
So all these neighbors
would come to our house

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:58.300
to watch "Wagon Train"
and "Woody Woodpecker,"

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.868
all those shows back then.

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:03.033
My daddy said, "We got to get
rid of this damn television."

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:05.934
But they would stay there, and
there were not late shows then.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:08.567
But the show would just go,
you know, just snow on it.

00:05:08.567 --> 00:05:12.467
So they'd stay there
and watch the late snow and...

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.067
-Just watching late snow.
-My daddy said,

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:18.400
"We got to get rid of this TV
because I got to work."

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.801
The people would just come,

00:05:19.801 --> 00:05:21.501
and you didn't want
to hurt their feelings.

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:23.200
-There's got to be some truth
to this thing.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:26.067
-Now, that is the truth.
I swear on that one.

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:29.067
That didn't have one of those
"Get Jimmy" buttons on it.

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:32.234
-No, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughs ]

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:34.534
This one says --

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.767
And I have a feeling
this is real, but I don't know.

00:05:36.767 --> 00:05:38.334
'Cause you're very cool.

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:41.267
You have a secret song
locked away in Dollywood

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.467
that will be released in 2045.

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:45.133
-That's the truth.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:46.534
No, seriously.

00:05:46.534 --> 00:05:49.000
When we -- We do a lot of things
at Dollywood,

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.667
and one year
we thought about that.

00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:53.367
They asked me
if I would write a song

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:56.534
that nobody would ever hear --
I'll be dead and gone.

00:05:56.534 --> 00:05:58.767
Well, I might not be
'cause I'll be 99.

00:05:58.767 --> 00:06:01.400
You know me.
I might still be hopping around.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.767
--Yeah, you'll be --
Yeah. I think --

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.000
You'll be there.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.901
-Anyway, I wrote a song,

00:06:07.901 --> 00:06:11.133
and I put it in the box
to be opened, and I even put --

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:13.767
Like, at that time
there was a CD player

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:15.701
and the ways in saying
what we were doing

00:06:15.701 --> 00:06:17.467
with our music at that time.

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:20.133
Left all the instructions and
here's how you can play this.

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:21.701
-No.
-I swear.

00:06:21.701 --> 00:06:23.334
And so I don't know
what they'll do with it.

00:06:23.334 --> 00:06:25.033
But I have regretted that.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:27.067
Because it was
a really good song.

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:28.567
[ Laughter ]
No, I'm serious.

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:30.267
-You could have released
that song.

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:32.200
-I keep wanting them
to let me dig it up

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.801
and put something else in it
that's not as good.

00:06:34.801 --> 00:06:37.167
-Yeah. 2045. We'll see the song.

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:39.467
-If any of you are around
when they open that box,

00:06:39.467 --> 00:06:41.501
well, I hope you enjoy my song.

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:45.234
-There you go. We will.
Dolly Parton, everybody.

00:06:45.234 --> 00:06:48.234
Check out "Dolly Parton's
Mountain Magic Christmas"

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:50.667
tomorrow night at 8:00 p.m.
on NBC.

00:06:50.667 --> 00:06:52.467
We'll be right back
with Claire Foy.

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:54.701
Stick around. No. I love you.

